{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Dwelling in safety, alone.</b> Each and every individual man under his vine and under his fig tree, scattered, and they do not need to gather and sit together because of the enemy." "<b>The eye of Jacob.</b> Like ״וְעֵינוֹ כְּעֵין הַבְּדֹלַח״ (Numbers 11) — like the eye of the blessing with which Jacob blessed them. Not like the בָּדָד that Jeremiah said: ״בָּדָד יָשַׁבְתִּי״ (Jeremiah 15), but like the eye of the assurance that Jacob assured them (Genesis 48): ״וְהָיָה אֱלֹהִים עִמָּכֶם וְהֵשִׁיב אֶתְכֶם אֶל אֶרֶץ אֲבֹתֵיכֶם״ (see Sifrei)." "<b>They shall drop.</b> They shall drip." "Also <b>His skies shall drop dew.</b> Also the blessing of Isaac is added upon the blessing of Jacob: ״וְיִתֶּן לְךָ הָאֱלֹהִים מִטַּל הַשָּׁמַיִם וְגוֹ׳״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:58.122118779Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}